        "original_id": "f05baae6-785c-524d-a32c-42a45cc1d32a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Live in London\n- People: Il Divo, Frank Matcham, Oswald Stoll\n- Organizations: London Philharmonic Orchestra\n- Places: London Coliseum, St. Martin's Lane, London\n\nFacts:\n- The London Coliseum opened on 24 December 1904 as the London Coliseum Theatre of Varieties.\n- Frank Matcham designed the London Coliseum for the impresario Oswald Stoll.\n- The London Coliseum is a theatre on St. Martin's Lane in central London and was built as one of London's largest and most luxurious family variety theatres.\n- On 1 August 2011, Il Divo performed a concert at the London Coliseum in London accompanied by the London Philharmonic Orchestra.\n- Live in London is a home video of Il Divo's 1 August 2011 concert at the London Coliseum in London.",
